{"ticker":"GSFC","symbol":"GSFC","instrumentId":3022931,"name":"Gsfc","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Agricultural","about":"Gujarat State Fertilizers & Chemicals Ltd. (GSFC) is a prominent player in the Indian fertilizers and chemicals industry, offering a diverse range of products such as fertilizers, petrochemicals, and industrial chemicals. Its fertilizer products, including urea, ammonium sulfate, and complex fertilizers, contribute significantly to India's agricultural growth. In addition, GSFC produces various industrial chemicals, like caprolactam, nylon-6, and melamine, catering to multiple sectors such as textiles, plastics, and construction. With a focus on sustainability and innovation, GSFC is committed to improving productivity in the agricultural and industrial sectors, ensuring high-quality products and services for its customers nationwide.","website":"www.gsfclimited.com","location":"INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:21:03.266Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":140.61,"changePct":0.7162810686913543,"week52High":190.82,"week52Low":133.28},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹5,603 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹13,898 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"247,056,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"190"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"73,121,918"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"3.56%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"0.46"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.9"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.11"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.23"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-10%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"10.01"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"4–22"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"5.5%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"3.42"},{"label":"Volume","value":"379,481"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"882,525"},{"label":"Master score","value":"37"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"27"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"25"},{"label":"Group rank","value